1581:### No process spawns
1582-
1583-vc-x1 runs jj and git through the jj-lib and gix libraries, never by spawning the `jj` or `git`
1584-binaries. The ban is enforced, and the exceptions are not: there is no allowlist. What exists is
1585-three things, and it pays to know which is which.
1586-
1587-- **The ban is config.** `clippy.toml` lists `std::process::Command::new` under
1588-  `disallowed-methods`, and `Cargo.toml` sets that lint to deny, so a bare call anywhere fails
1589-  `cargo clippy`, which `vc-x1 validate` runs.
1590-- **An exception is an attribute.** Clippy has no way to list permitted sites, so the only grant
1591-  is `#[allow(clippy::disallowed_methods)]` on the call itself, with a comment naming the entry
1592-  it claims. Nine sites carry one today.
1593-- **The register is prose.** The numbered comment at the top of `clippy.toml` names the five
